From 29146141289a8e62fcea98d310da14056242d2bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seddik Turki <mohamedseddik.turki@insat.ucar.tn>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 01:31:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix blocking bugs, restore stdout cap, add shared evaluator

- load_frames() never returned its result; both entry points crashed
- data_utils resolved src/rgbt-3m while main.py resolved <root>/rgbt-3m, so
  labels and images were read from different directories; R now has a single
  definition that everything imports
- rename rgbt-3/ -> rgbt-3m/ to match the code
- upload() was called with 2 of its 3 args in agentic/main.py
- imports were a mix of top-level and package-absolute and resolved from no
  entry point; now relative, run with python -m src.<method>.main
- restore the stdout cap in the agentic prompt (dropping it was worth ~13x on
  input tokens for one frame), note the thermal is non-radiometric, fix typos
- trace() ignored thinking blocks while thinking was enabled
- agentic: extract detect(), delete uploads in finally, cache_control on the
  first block, per-turn token/tool accounting
- add src/evaluation/metrics.py: shared mAP + centre-coverage, MAX_DETS=[1,10,300]
- .gitignore: pycache, artefacts, dataset files
